 KIP to propose this change?

Best,
Chia-Ping

On 2026/08/18 08:34:09 Alexander Neubeck wrote:
> Hi Kafka developers,
>=20
> KIP-32 describes LogAppendTime as monotonically increasing. However, the cu=
rrent implementation stamps records using the active leader=E2=80=99s local c=
lock.
>=20
> After a leader election, the new leader=E2=80=99s clock may be behind the p=
revious leader=E2=80=99s clock. In that case, newly appended records can rece=
ive a lower LogAppendTime than preceding records in the partition.
>=20
> A possible fix is for each partition leader to select:
>=20
> Plain text
>=20
> max(current broker time, previous LogAppendTime)
>=20
>=20
>=20
> The previous value can be recovered from the replicated log tail and mainta=
ined across follower appends, restart, truncation, and leader promotion. This=
 guarantees nondecreasing timestamps without forcing a one-millisecond increa=
se for every append.
>=20
> Would this be considered a correctness fix completing KIP-32=E2=80=99s inte=
nded monotonicity guarantee, or would the observable timestamp behavior requi=
re a follow-up KIP?
>=20
> KIP-32:
>=20
> https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-32+-+Add+timestamps+t=
o+Kafka+message
>=20
> Current assignment logic:
>=20
> https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/trunk/storage/src/main/java/org/apache=
/kafka/storage/internals/log/LogValidator.java
>=20
> Thanks,
>=20
> Alexander
>=20

