Subject: Webinar: Diskless Topics on Apache Kafka (Sept 21)
To: users@kafka.apache.org
Content-Type: multipart/alternative; boundary="00000000000000add7065b833986"
From: Hugh Evans <hugh.evans.dev@gmail.com>
Reply-To: <users@kafka.apache.org>

--00000000000000add7065b833986
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"

Hi all,

Aiven is running a live webinar on Diskless Topics on Monday, September 21.
I'm Hugh, Developer Advocate at Aiven, hosting it.

Diskless Topics move Kafka's replication from local disks to object
storage, which removes cross-AZ replication fees in cloud deployments. The
session covers the storage layer abstraction and pluggable leaders behind
it, then a live demo: creating a Diskless topic and switching an existing
classic topic over.

Times: 7am PDT / 10am EDT / 3pm BST / 4pm CEST / 7:30pm IST / 5pm EEST

Details and registration:
https://go.aiven.io/devrel-socials-kafka-diskless-topics

Happy to answer questions here if useful.

Hugh

--00000000000000add7065b833986--

