On Mon, Sep 28, 2026 at 11:46=E2=80=AFAM Lucas Brutschy via dev <
dev@kafka.apache.org> wrote:

> Hi Apoorv,
>
> +1 (binding)
>
> I covered much of the same ground Andrew and Bill already did and
> encountered no issues there either, so I won't repeat the details.
> Here is what I additionally checked, on macOS, JDK 21 (Temurin):
>
> * Verified the 4.2.2-rc1 git tag dereferences to commit
> c5e942859576203e1b00260070fe6241b64db251, which matches the commitId
> reported at broker startup by both the binary tarball and both Docker
> images.
> * I confirmed the currently staged kafka-clients-4.2.2.jar has
> Last-Modified 2026-09-22, consistent with the re-upload rather than a
> stale pre-drop copy.
> * Beyond the basic KIP-1071 smoke test, exercised
> kafka-streams-groups.sh end to end against a live streams group:
> --list, --describe --members/--state/--offsets/--verbose, and
> confirmed --reset-offsets --dry-run is rejected while the group is
> Stable and succeeds once it goes Empty.
> * Tested two specific fixes merged since 4.2.1:
>   - KAFKA-20685 (EOS checkpoint file not deleted after restoration):
> forced a full restoration under exactly_once_v2 and confirmed the
> checkpoint file is gone by the time the task eaches RUNNING.
>   - KAFKA-21096 (SharePartition metrics leak): confirmed via JMX that
> InFlightMessageCount, InFlightBatchCount and the related gauges/meters
> are properly deregistered once a SharePartition is fenced and removed
> from the cache (e.g. after the topic is deleted).
>
> Thanks Apoorv for running the release!
>
>
